  "canon:pmid": "12596116",
  "canon:title": "Octreotide-induced hypoxemia and pulmonary hypertension in premature neonates.",
  "canon:abstract": "The authors report 2 cases of premature neonates who had enterocutaneous fistula complicating necrotizing enterocolitis. Pulmonary hypertension developed after administration of a somatostatin analogue, octreotide, to enhance resolution of the fistula. The authors discuss the mechanism of the occurrence of this complication and recommend caution of its use in high-risk premature neonates.",
  "canon:text": "Octreotide-induced hypoxemia and pulmonary hypertension in premature neonates. The authors report 2 cases of premature neonates who had enterocutaneous fistula complicating necrotizing enterocolitis. Pulmonary hypertension developed after administration of a somatostatin analogue, octreotide, to enhance resolution of the fistula. The authors discuss the mechanism of the occurrence of this complication and recommend caution of its use in high-risk premature neonates.",
